\paragraph{Context and investigated scope.} The complete supplied definition, including source qualifications and the dated literature assessment, was reviewed. The calculation below is an elementary restricted attempt motivated by [S2]; it does not claim novelty or a fresh literature-status determination.

\paragraph{A long-wave failure visible in a dispersion relation.} In a constant-coefficient quasigeostrophic test model the linear equation $\partial_t(\Delta\psi-L_D^{-2}\psi)+\beta\partial_x\psi=0$ has plane-wave frequency
\[
 \omega(k,l)=-\frac{\beta k}{k^2+l^2+L_D^{-2}},
\]
obtained by substituting $e^{i(kx+ly-\omega t)}$. Put $K^2=k^2+l^2$ and $a=L_D^{-2}>0$. The short-wave expansion is $\omega=-(\beta k/K^2)\sum_{n\geq0}(-a/K^2)^n$, which converges only when $K^2>a$.

\paragraph{Quantifying the leading error.} With $\omega_0=-\beta k/K^2$ and $\beta k\ne0$, the relative frequency error is exactly $|\omega_0-\omega|/|\omega|=a/K^2$. It becomes large for the longest waves. Retaining $a$ in the denominator is a simple uniform repair for this test equation; it recovers the finite long-wave form $\omega\sim-\beta k/a$. At $\beta k=0$ with $K>0$, both frequencies vanish, so relative error is undefined and one must use absolute error. At $K=0$, the exact frequency is zero but the short-wave expression itself is undefined.

\paragraph{Source limitation.} This is not the report's global short-wave equatorial model, and the constant-coefficient approximation omits equatorial trapping and meridional mode structure. It therefore diagnoses a generic nonuniform denominator expansion rather than explaining the source discrepancy. The first gap is locating the corresponding discarded balance in the actual model and deriving a matched approximation with a norm and wavelength range. Its longest-wave errors remain unresolved by the illustrative calculation.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked plane-wave signs, geometric-series convergence, exact relative error and k=0; did not identify the test equation with the source model. Model self-audit only; no independent human proof checking. Prompts A and B were applied to this canonical record and its qualified source scope. Checked plane-wave signs, geometric-series convergence, exact relative error and k=0; did not identify the test equation with the source model. Retained unresolved status and zero original-target progress; The actual equatorial model has not been matched to a uniform long-wave approximation with controlled error.

Coordinator checked the dispersion expansion, exact relative-error formula and all zero-frequency cases, including the undefined constant-mode short-wave approximation. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 was used for file preparation and structural checks; no numerical experiment or theorem prover was used. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

\paragraph{Final status and first remaining gap.}
